@title How a building permit application is routed
@subtitle Whitcombe City planning office, for front-counter staff and applicants
@date 2026-10-01

## Routing flow

diagram route dir=TB title="Building permit routing"
route: start "Application received" svc focus
route: complete "Submission complete?" decision
route: ret "Return to applicant" ext
route: value "Project value over 50000 dollars?" decision
route: fast "Fast-track review" svc
route: hist "In a historic district?" decision
route: heritage "Heritage Board review" team
route: plan "Plan review" svc
route: issued "Permit issued" svc focus
route: start -> complete
route: complete -> ret : no
route: complete -> value : yes
route: value -> fast : no
route: value -> hist : yes
route: hist -> heritage : yes
route: hist -> plan : no
route: heritage -> plan : cleared
route: fast -> issued : approved
route: plan -> issued : approved

## Review times

table = stage,target; Completeness check,within 2 business days; Fast-track review,within 3 business days; Plan review,within 15 business days; Heritage Board review,"within 30 days, added on top of the plan review time"

## Fees

kpi Base fee | $180 | every application | neutral
kpi Value fee | 0.8% | of the project value above $50,000 | neutral

Every application pays the base fee of 180 dollars, plus 0.8 percent of the project value above 50000 dollars. For example, a 100000 dollar project pays 180 plus 400, which is 580 dollars.
